  "description": "QATLEF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H120 Fe4 Gd4 N8 O36,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1A (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2A (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.410-3.915 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.56-142.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C72H124Fe4Gd4N8O38. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
